@FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5138
# Paste the token returned by /api/auth/login here
@token = <jwt-from-login>

### Sign up as a food seeker (a verification email is sent)
POST {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/auth/sign-up/food-seeker
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}

### Log in (the account must be verified first)
POST {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}

### Active food items within 5 km, filtered by keyword
GET {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/food/nearby?latitude=41.0082&longitude=28.9784&distanceKm=5&keyword=soup
Accept: application/json

### Donators near a location
GET {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/donator/nearby?latitude=41.0082&longitude=28.9784
Accept: application/json

### Create a food item (Donator role)
POST {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/food
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lentil soup",
  "description": "Four portions left from lunch",
  "isEatIn": true,
  "isTakeAway": true,
  "isBringPack": false
}

### Request pickup of a food item (FoodSeeker role) - notifies the donator
POST {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/pickup-intent/1/send-notification
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My pickup intents
GET {{FoodSeekerAPI_HostAddress}}/api/pickup-intent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
